   "recapStatus": "Drafted",
   "recap": "Survivor 51 opened the Open Era with 21 players arriving as one group instead of ready-made tribes. Lewis Kelly volunteered to leave the group, spent about 30 hours on exile, failed a timed challenge to earn an idol, and learned he would join whichever tribe lost the first Tribal Council. The group split into yellow Toka and purple Savu. Kristin Flickinger and Danny \u201cKilby\u201d Kilby negotiated the opening supplies. Kristin won their thumb war and took the pot, flint, and machete bundle plus the fishing gear for Savu, while Kilby carried the building and shelter supplies back to Toka. Toka also received a pot, flint, and machete at camp after losing immunity, so both tribes ended up with supplies. At Savu, Rob Antonson found the first hidden immunity idol, with no Beware requirement and usable through the final five. Jeff Probst offered the cast a unanimous chance to abolish final-four firemaking; not everyone agreed, so it stayed in play. He also revealed that one player will face a coin flip later in the season, where a correct call grants safety, an idol, and an extra $1 million, and a miss sends that player out immediately and rolls the million into next season. Savu won immunity, sending Toka to the first Tribal Council with a \u201cSorry For You\u201d banner planted in their faces. Jenna Doore drew suspicion over her wedding photography story. Both Jenna and Aaliyah Puglia played Shot in the Dark, so neither cast a vote and neither gained safety. The eight counted votes fell 6 to 2, with Devin Way and Jelly Loblack voting for Jenna and the other six voting for Aaliyah. Aaliyah Puglia became the first person voted out of Survivor 51. The episode was dedicated to Survivor editor Finian Shea Johnson.",
